From: Zhenyu Li <48652137+JHSUYU@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:55:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Delete the discovered ports, their pairing and their
 carrier role

Nothing feeds them any more.  The demand walk stopped reading them in the
previous commit, and the one admission rule discarded 670 of 674 and 206
of 229 of what they proposed even before that, so what is deleted here is
the machinery for building a candidate the rule was always going to throw
away.

* cluster B, undeclared port discovery (470 lines): statePorts,
  addRuntimeAccess, accessorPorts, externalCallReturnPorts,
  exactAccessorReturnEvents, semanticExternalCallReturnEdges,
  returnEventKey, primitiveReturnType, staticAccessSiteId, containerRole,
  containerMutationPort, mutationOutputCells, copyRuntimeOccurrence,
  addUniqueValue, portId.  A region's ports are now its declared ones:
  the cut ports its case declared, and -- at PLAN -- the ports
  SymbolicInputSelection mints from the scope map's DECLARED_SITE rows
  and the recording's own captures.
* cluster C, the offline STATE pairing (419): fieldFlows, fieldFlowEdge,
  failureRelevantFields, collectPorts, boundedRuntimeAccesses,
  leafReceiverDemand, semanticHeapAddress, causalHeapPort,
  toolBookkeepingPort/Field, BoundPort, SemanticHeapAddress,
  RuntimeAccessDemand, MAX_RETAINED_SITE_ACCESSES.  Which write a read
  observed is the rows' answer (SlotTable), never an offline join on a
  recorded receiver.
* cluster E, the explicit-fault retention rule (375):
  retainExactRequestFaultControls, exactRequestFaultControlEdges,
  targetRequestProducerSources, fatalSharedLocationWriters,
  requestFaultControlEdge, sameOptionalValue, exchangeTransaction,
  explicitFaultPorts.  Inert already: its input was a
  RUNTIME_PROTOCOL_FLOW edge, and the pass that made those went with
  cluster D.  callReturnValueCells stays -- the declared cut ports
  (cluster H) name their value cell with it.
* with them: filterPorts, trimFatalPrefixAccesses, retainRuntimeAccesses,
  stampEdgeOccurrences, canonicalizeRegionEdges, the whole port half of
  RegionDemandIndex (inputs/outputs, inputsByInstance, inputsByBoundary,
  boundedMutationFrontiersByOutput, inputsForOutput, exploredSeeds,
  fatalPrefixContexts, which no stage read), ClosureWalk's three
  unreachable sets, Result.regionEdges and every consumer of it
  (RuntimeRegionPlanner's edge-validation loop, OccurrenceBinding
  .bindEdges, exactPort), and plan/AutomaticRegionEdge, whose only
  readers were those two files.
* DependencyRole.CONCRETE_STRUCTURE_CARRIER, DependencyRole.merge and the
  carrier stamps (RuntimeRegionPlanner.effectiveDependencyRole ->
  symbolicLeafPort, a boolean: can the VM present this value at all).  A
  plan artifact written before this change states a role this engine has
  no meaning for -- normalize refuses it by name -- and is not a
  supported input.  The kept gate corpora's plan artifacts are not
  re-read by wave0 or compose (wave0 reads the corpus sessions and the
  scope map, compose reads the sessions), confirmed by both being
  byte-identical across this change.
* the CONCRETE-row production has no producer left on either corpus: the
  published inputActions are now 100% SYMBOLIC / VALUE_FRONTIER (17960 4,
  11741 46), where the previous commit still published 46 and 12 CONCRETE
  rows and PC3 published 670 and 206.  addConcreteInputAction stays for
  the two refusals that are not policy -- a location the VM has no
  presentation for, a type the SMT layer has no term for -- now asked
  only of a DECLARED port.

Readers of every deleted published member, checked with git grep on the
staging tip 0e3c1ab39 and on the in-flight branches r3/C3 and r3/FIX1:
all of them are in RuntimeSelectedRegionFinalizer, RuntimeRegionPlanner,
OccurrenceBinding, CausynthTraceRecorder, DependencyRole,
AutomaticRegionEdge and this test.  No caller in either /opt/hadoop-* tree.
StaticProgram.regionEdges stays: SymbolicRegionPlanner:114 still clears
it (a handoff, not mine).

RuntimeSelectedRegionFinalizer 3702 -> 1634 lines.

Gate (rc=0, 0 SKIPPED): task counts and the symbolize sets are unmoved
from the previous commit -- 17960 rows=16 symbolize=4
[OBSERVED_FIELD_RECEIVER:4], 11741 rows=133 symbolize=46
[CALL_RETURN:16, COMMUNICATION_SITE_PORT:30] -- and every wave0, compose
and meta row is byte-identical.  The three plan digests per corpus move
because the rows no longer carry the discarded candidates, and the task
ids with them.  17960/static/candidate_dataflow_edges.jsonl.gz moves by
the known Soot local-naming instability alone: rows=8833 both, no id
gained or lost, 6 guard_dependency rows in one method
(INodesInPath.resolvePath) differing by the single transposition
$z5 <-> $z6, (kind,siteId) multiset identical ($MY/r3/cdecheck.py).

The cluster-E test slot is repointed at the rule that replaced it: a
declared attach is named by the declaration joined with the recording's
capture, never by the wire transaction.

